        "email": "119861875+VictorKuang25@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-20T09:37:59Z"
      },
      "message": "[Enh] Replace vector<bool> with uint8_t to remove per-point mutex in BuildResidualListOMP\n\nIn BuildResidualListOMP, every iteration of the #pragma omp parallel for loop previously acquired a shared per-call std::mutex (mylock) to write useful_ptpl[i] and all_ptpl_list[i], serializing parallel residual construction.\n\nBecause voxel_map_ and octree nodes are accessed read-only and build_single_residual only writes to stack locals and pv_list[i].normal, each index i is independent once bit-packed std::vector<bool> (which cannot be written concurrently at adjacent indices without locking) is replaced by std::vector<uint8_t>(pv_list.size(), 0).\n\nAlso value-initialize PointToPlane single_ptpl{} so copying single_ptpl into all_ptpl_list[i] does not load uninitialized bool is_valid_ (which triggers UBSan invalid-bool-load UB without modifying include/voxel_map.h).\n\nOutput is bit-for-bit identical: the main thread still collects results sequentially in i = 0 .. N-1 order.",
