        "date": "2026-11-20T09:38:07Z"
      },
      "message": "[Fix] Fix heap leak, null/uninitialized pointers, and stale G in VIO\n\nOutput-preserving memory-safety and defensive fixes in VIO:\n\n- visual_point.cpp (VisualPoint::VisualPoint): initialize ref_patch to nullptr\n  in the constructor so deleteFeatureRef() and precomputeReferencePatches()\n  never inspect an uninitialized member pointer.\n- vio.cpp (updateVisualMapPoints): move new float[patch_size_total] and\n  getImagePatch() inside if (add_flag); previously patch_temp (256 B for 8x8)\n  was leaked every frame for every tracked point where add_flag was false.\n- vio.cpp (precomputeReferencePatches): check pt == nullptr,\n  pt->ref_patch == nullptr, and img.empty() before dereferencing\n  pt->ref_patch->img_.\n- vio.cpp (retrieveFromVisualSparseMap): initialize Feature *ref_ftr = nullptr,\n  defensively skip candidates with count == 0 before dividing by count, and\n  skip dereferencing when ref_ftr is null.\n- vio.cpp (computeJacobianAndUpdateEKF): call G.setZero() before the pyramid\n  loop so state->cov -= G * state->cov cannot reuse a stale or uninitialized G\n  if no pyramid level accepts an update.\n- vio.cpp (updateStateInverse): cleanup matching updateState by materializing\n  solution as MD(DIM_STATE, 1) instead of auto to avoid redundant Eigen\n  expression re-evaluation.",
