        "date": "2026-11-20T09:38:07Z"
      },
      "message": "[Fix] Fix uninitialized means, unreset NCC, and OOB image reads in VIO\n\nFixes active undefined behavior and out-of-bounds memory accesses in VIO\n(these fixes intentionally alter outputs that were previously corrupted by\nuninitialized memory reads, accumulated NCC state, or OOB pixels):\n\n- updateReferencePatch:\n  * Initialize ref_mean and other_mean from cached Feature::mean_. Previously\n    both were uninitialized locals only assigned when abs(mean_) < 1e-6; since\n    the inner loop of the first outer iteration caches mean_ for all other\n    observations, every outer iteration from the 2nd onward read uninitialized\n    stack garbage on every call.\n  * Move NCC_up, NCC_down1, NCC_down2 inside the inner pair loop so each pair\n    starts from 0.0 rather than accumulating across previous pairs.\n  * Guard sqrt(NCC_down1 * NCC_down2) > 1e-6f and count > 0 against div-by-zero.\n- updateState, updateStateInverse, precomputeReferencePatches,\n  updateVisualMapPoints:\n  * Add file-local helpers isPatchInBounds() and isRefPatchValid() (no vio.h\n    changes) enforcing exact pixel access bounds ([0, +scale] for bilinear-only,\n    [-scale, +2*scale] for central-difference gradients) plus range/finiteness\n    checks before float-to-int conversion and pf[2] <= 0 guards. With default\n    patch_size=8 and patch_pyrimid_level=3, border=40 px while updateState can\n    reach scale=1<<(2+2)=16 (80 px footprint), triggering heap-buffer-overflow\n    near image borders.\n  * Share isRefPatchValid() between precomputeReferencePatches() and\n    updateStateInverse() so skipped points are consistent and do not dilute\n    error / n_meas with zero-Jacobian residuals.\n  * Reset z and H_sub at the start of each iteration to prevent stale rows\n    when points are skipped on later iterations, and restore old_state + break\n    when n_meas == 0 before dividing error / n_meas.",
