      },
      "message": "[Fix] Prevent repeated motion compensation of first point in ImuProcess::UndistortPcl\n\nThe inner backward-propagation loop breaks upon reaching pcl_wait_proc.points.begin(),\nbut does not exit the outer IMUpose loop. Whenever\npoints[0].curvature / 1000.0 > IMUpose[1].offset_time (i.e., the first retained\npoint is later than the first IMU measurement in the scan, e.g., after blind-range\nor point_filter_num culling or scan splitting), points[0] satisfies\ncurvature / 1000.0 > head->offset_time again on every earlier IMU interval and gets\nmotion-compensated multiple times.\n\nTrack completion with all_done to break both loops once points.begin() is processed.",
